from pathlib import Path
import json
folder=Path('outputs/shared_pressure_observations_20261030')
lines=['# Additional local PDE observations: stationary audit','', 'These experiments change local Hermite observations and their matching representers. They do not add independent global PDE test equations. Velocity, pressure and boundary groups retain their nearest-37 original physical sites; two or four off-node PDE sites are then added per patch. In the replacement variant, the original nodal PDE samples are omitted and only four off-node PDE samples remain.', '', 'All runs use velocity degree 6 / pressure degree 2, viscosity 0.01, the existing fully scaled kernels, C++ 80-digit weights and two MPI ranks. Global assembly and row-equilibrated SVD use Float64. Pressure mean is the proposed gauge. The additional PDE data are stationary forcing values; no unsteady closure or time integration is claimed.', '', '| Artifact | Nodes | Extra sites | Replace original PDE samples | Numerical nullity | xy momentum residual | Smooth momentum residual | Smooth pressure residual |', '| --- | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
for path in sorted(folder.glob('*.json')):
 d=json.loads(path.read_text())
 if 'diagnostics' not in d: continue
 xy,smooth=d['results'][0],d['results'][2]
 lines.append(f"| [{path.name}]({path.name}) | {d['total_nodes']} | {d['extra_momentum_sites_per_patch']} | {d['replace_original_momentum']} | {d['diagnostics']['numerical_nullity']} | {xy['exact_momentum_defect']:.3e} | {smooth['exact_momentum_defect']:.3e} | {smooth['exact_pressure_defect']:.3e} |")
lines += ['', 'The tested variants retain extra numerical null directions. The solver therefore does not fabricate a unique solution or report nodal solution errors. Listed residuals substitute the exact nodal fields into the assembled equations; they are consistency defects, not solved-field errors or evidence of evolution stability.', '', 'The smooth test uses streamfunction sin(pi*x)^2 sin(pi*y)^2, velocity (d_y psi, -d_x psi), and pressure sin(pi*x) sin(pi*y). Its forcing was independently checked against symbolic derivatives. The polynomial test additionally exercises nonzero boundary velocity (x^2,-2xy) with pressure xy.', '', 'Each NPZ file saves the associated sparse matrix for subsequent rank/scaling analysis. No regularization, least-squares selection, pressure boundary data, or Q2/Q1 space was introduced.']
(folder/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
